Linktext.mcc/Linktext.mcc

   Linktext.mcc is a Zune custom class derived from MUIC_Area. It shows
   read-only text that wraps and scrolls, with links inside its paragraphs.
   A link wraps with the text around it, and has its own target, so its
   label can differ from the address it stands for.

   The application gives plain text and explicit spans. A span covers bytes
   of the text and either makes them a link (it has a target) or only sets
   their style. The class does not look for addresses in the text and does
   not parse a target. It opens nothing itself: it starts no browser, runs
   no Shell command and makes no network request. It reports what the user
   asked for through MUIA_Linktext_ActionHook, and the application decides.

   Text is one byte per character in the system's 8-bit character set, as
   for Text() and Floattext. Offsets count those bytes, and UTF-8 must be
   converted first. A newline ends a paragraph. Any other control character
   is shown as a space. No escape codes are interpreted.

   Mouse: a click on a link opens it. A drag selects text without opening
   anything, also when it starts on a link. The context menu opens or copies
   the link under the pointer, or copies the selection. A bubble shows the
   whole target of the link under the pointer.

   Keyboard, when the object is active: Left and Right go from link to link,
   Return opens, Amiga+C copies the link or else the selection, Up, Down and
   the page keys scroll, and Tab goes on to the next object in the window.

   Links are drawn in the text pen and underlined, with the font and pens
   of the user's preferences. A selection uses the fill and shine pens.
Linktext.mcc/MUIA_Linktext_ActionHook

   MUIA_Linktext_ActionHook -- [ISG], struct Hook *

   Called for each action, with the object and a
   struct MUI_LinktextAction *:

       Action        MUIV_Linktext_Action_Open or MUIV_Linktext_Action_Copy
       Link          which link, in text order; style spans are not counted
       ID            the span's ID
       Target        the span's target
       TargetLength  its length in bytes
       Qualifier     of the click or key; 0 from the context menu

   The hook runs on the application's task, inside the object's event
   handling. Target stays valid until the hook returns, even if the hook
   replaces the content; copy it to keep it. The hook may replace the
   content and close the window. To dispose the object use
   MUIM_Application_PushMethod.

   Return TRUE when handled. For Copy, FALSE makes the class copy Target to
   clipboard unit 0 itself, which is also what happens without a hook.
Linktext.mcc/MUIA_Linktext_First

   MUIA_Linktext_First -- [.SG], ULONG

   The wrapped line at the top. A value past the end shows the last lines.
Linktext.mcc/MUIA_Linktext_FixHeight

   MUIA_Linktext_FixHeight -- [I..], BOOL

   Makes the object exactly MUIA_Linktext_Lines high instead of stretching.
   Text that needs more lines scrolls by wheel and keyboard. Default FALSE.
Linktext.mcc/MUIA_Linktext_LineCount

   MUIA_Linktext_LineCount -- [..G], ULONG

   Wrapped lines at the current width, 0 before the object was first shown.
Linktext.mcc/MUIA_Linktext_Lines

   MUIA_Linktext_Lines -- [I.G], ULONG

   Lines of text to ask for in the default height. Default 4.
Linktext.mcc/MUIA_Linktext_Scroller

   MUIA_Linktext_Scroller -- [I..], Object *

   A Scrollbar or Prop object to keep in step, as MUIA_TextEditor_Slider
   does. The object must outlive this one or be disposed with it; this class
   does not dispose it.
Linktext.mcc/MUIM_Linktext_LinkBox

   DoMethod(obj, MUIM_Linktext_LinkBox, ULONG Link, ULONG Fragment,
            struct IBox *Box);

   Where a link is on screen now, for tests and for placing a hint. A link
   has one fragment per line it reaches. Box gets the place of that fragment
   in window coordinates. Returns TRUE when the fragment exists and is at
   least partly visible. FALSE with Box unchanged when there is no such
   fragment; FALSE with Box set when it is scrolled out of view.
Linktext.mcc/MUIM_Linktext_SetContent

   ULONG DoMethod(obj, MUIM_Linktext_SetContent, CONST_STRPTR Text,
                  ULONG Length, const struct MUI_LinktextSpan *Spans,
                  ULONG SpanCount);

   Replaces the whole content, at once or not at all, and returns a
   MUIV_Linktext_Status_*. On any failure the content shown before stays and
   nothing changes. The object copies the text and the targets during the
   call, so nothing passed in needs to outlive it.

   Text may be NULL for none. Length is in bytes; ~0UL means up to the first
   NUL. Each span has:

       Start   byte offset into the text
       Length  bytes, at least 1
       Flags   MUIV_Linktext_Span_Bold or 0
       Target  NUL-terminated text, kept exactly; NULL for a style span
       ID      the application's, handed back in actions

   Spans come in text order and do not overlap. Several links may share a
   target or an ID. A target is any non-empty text.

   Result:

       MUIV_Linktext_Status_OK
       MUIV_Linktext_Status_Range     a span outside the text, or empty
       MUIV_Linktext_Status_Order     spans overlap or are out of order
       MUIV_Linktext_Status_Target    a link with an empty target
       MUIV_Linktext_Status_TooLarge  over a limit below
       MUIV_Linktext_Status_NoMemory

   Limits: LINKTEXT_MAX_TEXT bytes of text (64 MiB), LINKTEXT_MAX_SPANS spans
   (1000000), LINKTEXT_MAX_TARGET bytes per target (16 MiB).
